# site/module-{{ id }}

{{ Title }}: a section of this site's panel, kept in the site's repository in `modules/{{ id }}`
and installed by Composer as a path package (a symlink in `vendor/site/module-{{ id }}`). It is
built exactly like a packaged WebX UI module, so it can move into one by moving the folder and
renaming three things: the vendor `site`, the namespace `Site\` and the npm scope `@site`.

## What it owns

- **Table** `{{ table }}` (`Site\{{ Studly }}\Models\{{ Model }}`). `title` is translatable;
  `position` is the one order of the list; `extra` holds fields a patch adds to the form.
- **Panel screen** `{{ id }}.form` (nodes `main`, `title`); help `{{ id }}.index`, `{{ id }}.form` in
  `resources/help/<language>`.
- **API** under `/api/cms/{{ id }}`: list, one record, create, save, delete, `reorder`.
- **MCP** tools `{{ tool }}_list`, `{{ tool }}_get`, `{{ tool }}_create`, `{{ tool }}_update`,
  `{{ tool }}_delete`, `{{ tool }}_reorder`; resource `{{ id }}://catalog`. Scopes `{{ id }}:read`,
  `{{ id }}:write`.
- **Words** under `webx-{{ id }}` (`lang/<language>`), English and the languages of the site's panel.
- **Front end** `@site/module-{{ id }}` in `js/`: `{{ function }}()` with the list and the form,
  built by the site's Vite from its sources — there is no `dist`.
- Also registered: demo content (`resources/demo/{{ id }}.json`), the table for `webx:snapshot`,
  the ready-made roles (`editor` writes, `seo` reads).

### Permissions

| Permission         | Opens                                                         |
| ------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `{{ id }}.view`   | the list and the form, read-only; `{{ tool }}_list`, `{{ tool }}_get` |
| `{{ id }}.manage` | create, edit, reorder and delete; the `{{ id }}:write` tools   |

## Change it

| You want                         | Do this                                                                                  |
| -------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| A new field of a {{ model }}     | a column (migration + model), a node in `resources/screens/form.json`, its line of help in every language, the name in `OWN` of `{{ Model }}Form` |
| A field only for this site       | a patch onto `{{ id }}.form`; it is saved in `extra` without a column                   |
| Another word in the panel        | the same key in `lang/en` and every other language, and in `js/src/messages.ts`          |
| A new dependency or provider     | edit `composer.json` here, then `composer update site/module-{{ id }}`                   |

## Do not

- Do not edit `vendor/site/module-{{ id }}`: it is a link to this folder. Edit here.
- Do not give the module an id a packaged module has (`webx:modules`): two owners of one set of
  tables and permissions. `webx:doctor` says so.
- Do not add a route without `cms.can`, or a tool without a permission: `tests/AccessCoverageTest.php` fails.
- Do not put `@webx-ui/*` or `vue` into `dependencies` of `js/package.json`: they come from the site.

## Check your work

- `php artisan test --testsuite=Modules` — access, help, translations, MCP dry runs, budgets, CRUD.
- `npm run typecheck:modules` and `npm run test:modules`.
- `php artisan webx:doctor`; open the section in the panel.
- With MCP: read `{{ id }}://catalog` first; every tool that changes something takes `dry_run: true`.

